        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(google): Veo video generation fails with google-prefixed model ids",
        "body": "Closes #103291\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where calling the Google video generation provider with a `google/`-prefixed Veo model id (e.g. `google/veo-3.1-fast-generate-preview`) sends the request to the invalid path `models/google/veo-3.1-fast-generate-preview:predictLongRunning`, producing an `API_KEY_INVALID`-style error instead of the correct `models/veo-3.1-fast-generate-preview:predictLongRunning` endpoint.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe GenAI SDK treats any model id that does not start with `models/` or `tunedModels/` as `models/<input>`, so a bare `google/veo-3.1-fast-generate-preview` becomes `models/google/veo-3.1-fast-generate-preview`. The provider now normalizes Veo video model ids to the bare form before both the SDK call and the REST fallback, ensuring both paths hit `models/veo-...:predictLongRunning`.\n\n## User Impact\n\nUsers can now use `google/veo-3.1-fast-generate-preview`, `google/models/veo-3.1-fast-generate-preview`, or `veo-3.1-fast-generate-preview` interchangeably for Google video generation.\n\n## Evidence\n\n### Shared-runtime regression\n\nAdded `src/video-generation/runtime.test.ts` regression verifying that the shared runtime strips the provider prefix from `google/veo-3.1-fast-generate-preview` and forwards the bare model id to the provider.\n\n### Provider behavior proof (before / after)\n\nRan a temporary harness that exercises the real provider code path with a stubbed API key and intercepts the outgoing HTTP request. The URL below is exactly what the provider would send to Google.\n\n**Before this change** (reverting `extensions/google/video-generation-provider.ts` to `HEAD~1`):\n```text\n[URL-PROOF] https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta/models/google/veo-3.1-fast-generate-preview:predictLongRunning\n```\n\n**After this change** (current branch):\n```text\n[URL-PROOF] https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta/models/veo-3.1-fast-generate-preview:predictLongRunning\n```\n\nThe API key was redacted; no real Google account, private endpoint, IP, or project id appears in the output.\n\n### Test / check output\n\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/google/video-generation-provider.test.ts` — 18 tests passed\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/video-generation/runtime.test.ts` — 29 tests passed\n- `oxfmt` and `oxlint` clean on changed files\n\n### Note on live API proof\n\nI do not have a live Google API key available in this environment, so the before/after above uses the real provider code path with intercepted HTTP. If a maintainer can provide a redacted live run log, I am happy to append it.\n\n@clawsweeper re-review",
